==========================================================================
  VERDICT (delay): INCONCLUSIVE but directional, and NOT symmetric between the hypotheses. Neither coefficient clears alpha = 0.05 at n = 16 (df = 12). b_a = +0.0678 [-0.0420, +0.1775], p = 0.203 — point estimate runs AGAINST H1' (H1' predicts b_a < 0). b_s = -0.1105 [-0.2337, +0.0126], p = 0.074 — H2's direction. Largest standardised effect: s (beta* = -0.440). Availability remains flat (b_a p = 0.611), a third independent replication of it. Read as: H1' gained no support even with its confound removed, the residual signal is selectivity and general robustness, and the design is underpowered to separate a modest H2 effect from none.
